WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.100
In 2025, using market exchange rates,
America's economy was worth 30.86 trillion

2
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:07.870
dollars.

3
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.590
China's was worth 19.63 trillion.

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.650
Now adjust for what money
buys in each country.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.530
At purchasing power parity, China's
economy is 41.26 trillion dollars.

6
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.010
America's stays the same.

7
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.010
Same year.

8
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.570
Same IMF data.

9
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.090
Two different leaders.

10
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.610
So which country is the superpower?

11
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.410
The USA, China, both, or neither?

12
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.910
In this mission, you'll
measure power three ways:

13
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.490
economic, geopolitical and cultural,
and tell hard power from soft.

14
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.910
You'll weigh the dollar,
military spending,

15
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.970
exports and the Belt and Road, then
fill a scorecard dimension by dimension.

16
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.010
Your mission: decide which
country is the superpower,

17
00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.360
and back it with dated figures.
